Allow EGL_OPENGL_API in an Android (bionic) build of Mesa EGL.

Upstream rejects desktop GL on Android because the Android platform EGL has no GL
consumer. This build is an X11-platform EGL loaded by Wine's winex11 EGL backend,
whose WGL needs desktop GL (Zink gives 4.6 compat). Without this every
eglBindAPI(EGL_OPENGL_API) fails and Wine finds no GL context.

--- a/src/egl/main/eglcurrent.h
+++ b/src/egl/main/eglcurrent.h
@@ -66,7 +66,7 @@
 static inline EGLBoolean
 _eglIsApiValid(EGLenum api)
 {
-#if HAVE_OPENGL && !DETECT_OS_ANDROID
+#if HAVE_OPENGL
    /* OpenGL is not a valid/supported API on Android */
    if (api == EGL_OPENGL_API)
       return true;
